=== Ritual Casting ===

Ritual Casting is a quality-of-life feature added to EQ Legends.  It is not exclusively used for travel purposes, but travel is one of it's major uses.  Ritual Casting allows characters to cast some spells from classes which are ''not'' active in their current loadout ''if'' they have the class leveled high enough for the spell in question.  All wizard and druid self-only ports and group ports are included among the spells that can be used by this feature.  That means if you have either a wizard or a druid (or both) leveled enough to have their port spells, you will be able to cast them from any loadout.

For example, as a Level 12 Warrior/Monk/Rogue, you could use a Ritual to cast West Commons Gate, a level 21 Wizard Spell, if you have previously leveled a Wizard to level 21 or higher.

When using Rituals, you must be in a resting state (out of combat). The cast time for all Rituals is 20 seconds, and you will lose all Mana and Endurance when it completes casting.

Other notable spells that are available with Ritual Casting are [[Bind Affinity]] and [[Shrink]]

